; expect 42
; An effect declared in another module, performed under both spellings
; a reference to it can take.
;
; The evidence slot is named after the effect's MODULE as well as its
; name - `__axiom_ev_EffOps$Ask` - because two modules may each declare
; a `Console` and stage0 keys their slots by (name, module). Both
; spellings below have to reach that one slot: an operation registered
; only under its bare name emits a call to an undefined `@EffOps$ask`,
; and one registered only under the qualified name leaves `(ask 20)`
; undefined.
;
; The qualified spelling is why this case exists. stage1 resolves
; `EffOps::ask` by mangling it flat into `EffOps$ask`, which works for
; every other declaration because `mangleDecl` rewrote the declaration
; to match - and `effect` is one of the two kinds it does not rewrite.
; So a program stage0 compiles and runs drew a false
; `AX3001 undefined variable EffOps$ask` here.
(import EffOps)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (handle (+
    (ask 20)    (EffOps::ask
      1
    )
  ) (Ask) (lambda (x) (* x 2)))
)
